{% call section("Research", "research") %}
<p><i>AI safety.</i> How AI agents represent the world, value outcomes, and act, and how to make them safe: value learning and alignment, causal reasoning, and automated safety research. With <a href="https://www.danielherrmann.ca/">Daniel Herrmann</a> I co-direct <a href="https://exproof.ai/"><span class="exists" aria-hidden="true">&exist;</span><span class="visually-hidden">E</span>xProof AI</a>.</p>
<p><i>Metascience.</i> How scientific communities produce knowledge, and how to do it better: grant funding, replication and reform, and the social epistemology of science.</p>
<p><i>Methods.</i> Bayesian epistemology, decision theory, and evolutionary game theory, and the limits of these tools themselves.</p>
<p>Current funding: I am Principal Investigator on the Templeton-funded project <i>Identifying Breakthrough Science: Modeling, Measurement, and Funding Implications</i>, with Kevin Zollman and Simon DeDeo.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call section("Teaching and mentoring", "teaching") %}
<p>I teach decision theory, game theory, AI safety, logic, and philosophy of science at Carnegie Mellon; the full list is on the <a href="{{ '/teaching/' | url }}">Teaching</a> page. I mentor AI safety researchers through <a href="https://sparai.org/">SPAR</a> and advise master&rsquo;s students.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call section("Public writing", "writing") %}
<p>I write philosophy posts on <a href="https://www.lesswrong.com/users/aydin-mohseni">LessWrong</a>, among them <a href="https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/auSfqhbMKEvzt4unG/chance-is-in-the-map-not-the-territory">Chance is in the Map, not the Territory</a> and <a href="https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/qQTXjpXbcXMHvExmf/evolution-and-the-low-road-to-nash">Evolution and the Low Road to Nash</a>.</p>
{% endcall %}

